In nvme_trans_inquiry, inq_response is kmalloc'd with size alloc_len, which is the attacker-controlled 16-bit ALLOCATION LENGTH from the INQUIRY CDB (can be 0..65535). But several VPD/standard helpers write fixed-size data into that buffer regardless of alloc_len: standard, supported-VPD and serial pages memset/write 36 bytes, the device-id page writes up to 76 bytes (offset 56 + 20-byte serial) on its scsi_string path, and the block-limits page copies 0x3c=60 bytes out of it. With alloc_len smaller than these sizes (e.g. 0), this is a heap buffer overflow on write and an over-read on copy-to-user.</root_cause>
